# NuGet publish is pipeline-only

Do not deploy packages to nuget.org or GitHub Packages from this workspace.

This applies to **every plugin submodule** (LeakAnalyser, HttpForge, GeoLocator, and the rest), the UIKit hub module (`NuvyntraLabs.UIKit`), the NuvexaDB hub module (`Nuventra.NuvexaDB`), the Nuvyn CLI (`NuvyntraLabs.Nuvyn.Cli`), and Pulse (`Plugin.Maui.Pulse` + `Plugin.Maui.Pulse.Cli`).

- Do not run `dotnet nuget push`, pack-and-upload, or any other local feed push
- Do not use a local `NUGET_KEY` to publish
- Bump `Version` / `PackageVersion` in the plugin csproj and update docs here
- Publishing happens when that plugin repo's GitHub Actions CI runs (push to the plugin `main`, tag, or hub dispatch)
- A plugin repo may ship several nupkgs (library + PackAsTool `.Cli`, templates, source generators). Keep their `Version` values aligned. Tool packages omit snupkg.
- Each successful publish job pushes to nuget.org (`NUGET_KEY` for Plugin.Maui.*, `NUGET_KEY_UIKIT` for NuvyntraLabs.UIKit, `NUGET_KEY_NUVYN` for NuvyntraLabs.Nuvyn.Cli, `NUGET_KEY_WPF` for Plugin.Wpf.*, `NUGET_KEY_WINUI` for Plugin.WinUI.*, `NUGET_KEY_AVALONIA` for Plugin.Avalonia.*, `NUGET_KEY_UNO` for Plugin.Uno.*) and GitHub Packages (`GITHUB_TOKEN`). NuvexaDB packs nupkg + snupkg from `NuvexaDB/.github/workflows/ci.yml` and uploads them as GitHub artifacts; nuget.org / GitHub Packages push is commented out until multi-host publishing is decided. Nuvyn is PackAsTool (`net10.0` nupkg only) from `Nuvyn/.github/workflows/ci.yml`.

The hub repo does not publish packages. See `docs/getting-started.md` (Continuous integration).
